// ---- demos/markdown_view.qwe ----------------------------------------------------------------

let markdown_view_demo_text = `# Writing a component

Each component is **one file** you copy into your program. It brings its *own styles*,
follows the system's _light or dark_ theme, and ~~needs a build step~~ works as it is.
See [the gallery](https://quillolang.org/components/ "Quillo UI") for every one.

## What goes in

1. A comment saying what it is
2. Its CSS, as \`let name_css = css\`
3. The \`view\` or \`component\`

> Views first: a component with nothing to remember is a view.
> It is built on what the browser already does.

- [x] Read the README
- [ ] Write the test
- Press **Tab** to reach everything, and \\*escaped\\* stars stay

\`\`\`sh
scripts/build.sh && scripts/test.sh button
\`\`\`

---

Tags are shown as written: <script>alert(1)</script> and <b>not bold</b>.
A line that ends in two spaces  
breaks here. A [bad link](javascript:alert(1)) is blocked, and ![a picture](https://example.com/x.png) is text unless images are on.`

component MarkdownViewDemoLive() {
    state text = "Type some **Markdown** here, with a [link](https://quillolang.org) and `code`."
    <div.demo-stack>
        <TextArea name="markdown-view-demo-input" label="Markdown" rows={3} value={text} on_input={(t) => { text = t }}/>
        <div style="padding: 12px 14px; border: 1px solid var(--ui-border); border-radius: var(--ui-radius-sm)">
            <MarkdownView text={text} id="markdown-view-demo-live"/>
        </div>
    </div>
}

view MarkdownViewDemo() =
    <div.demo-stack>
        <MarkdownView text={markdown_view_demo_text} id="markdown-view-demo-doc"/>
        <MarkdownViewDemoLive/>
    </div>

